\begin_layout Abstract
The bounce action-angle coordinates for charged particles trapped in an
 axisymmetric dipole magnetic field are given.
 First, we present the bounce action-angle coordinates for deeply-trapped
 particles and we explicitly recover the Hamiltonian dynamics of a harmonic
 oscillator whose (bounce) frequency is a function of the guiding-center
 invariants.
 Next, we use the Lie-transform perturbation method to derive higher-order
 action-angle corrections.
 Lastly, we obtain explicit expressions for the bounce-center coordinates
 based on the existence of explicit expressions 
\begin_inset Formula $s(J,\zeta)$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $p_{\|}(J,\zeta)$
\end_inset

 for the lowest-order parallel dynamics.
 
\end_layout

