\begin_layout Standard
Lastly, it is worth pointing out that when the bounce period (
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "eq:tau_b_xi"

\end_inset

) is compared with the equatorial gyration period 
\begin_inset Formula $\tau_{\mathrm{g}}\equiv(pc/qB_{\mathrm{e}})\;\sqrt{1-\xi_{\mathrm{e}}^{2}}$
\end_inset

 and the equatorial bounce-averaged drift period 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation}
\tau_{\mathrm{d}}\;\equiv\;\left(\frac{4\pi}{3}\right)\frac{r_{\mathrm{e}}^{2}}{\rho_{\mathrm{e}}v}\; g(\xi_{\mathrm{e}}),\label{eq:tau_d_xi}\end{equation}

\end_inset

 where the normalized function 
\begin_inset Formula $g(\xi_{\mathrm{e}})$
\end_inset

 is shown in Fig.
\begin_inset space ~
\end_inset


\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "fig:g_xi"

\end_inset

, we obtain three well-separated orbital time scales 
\begin_inset Formula $\tau_{\mathrm{g}}\ll\tau_{\mathrm{b}}\ll\tau_{\mathrm{d}}$
\end_inset

 when 
\begin_inset Formula $\epsilon\;\equiv\;\rho_{\mathrm{e}}/r_{\mathrm{e}}\ll1$
\end_inset

 for all values of 
\begin_inset Formula $\xi_{\mathrm{e}}$
\end_inset

.
 Note that, by using Eq.
\begin_inset space ~
\end_inset

(
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "eq:phi_dot"

\end_inset

), the bounce-averaged drift frequency 
\begin_inset Formula $\langle\dot{\phi}\rangle_{\mathrm{b}}$
\end_inset

 can be expressed as 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\langle\dot{\phi}\rangle_{\mathrm{b}}\;\equiv\;\frac{1}{\tau_{\mathrm{b}}}\;\oint\frac{ds}{v_{\|}}\;\dot{\phi}\;=\;\frac{c\mu}{q}\;\left\langle \pd B{\psi}\right\rangle _{\mathrm{b}},\]

\end_inset

 where the bounce average of the second term in Eq.
\begin_inset space ~
\end_inset

(
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "eq:phi_dot"

\end_inset

) vanishes identically.
 For deeply-trapped particles 
\begin_inset Formula $(\xi_{\mathrm{e}}\ll1)$
\end_inset

, the bounce-averaged drift frequency is approximately given as 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation}
\langle\dot{\phi}\rangle_{\mathrm{b}}\;\simeq\;\frac{c\mu}{q}\;\pd{B_{\mathrm{e}}}{\psi_{\mathrm{e}}}\;=\;3\;\frac{c\mu}{qr_{\mathrm{e}}^{2}}\;\simeq\;\frac{3}{2}\;\frac{\rho_{\mathrm{e}}v}{r_{\mathrm{e}}^{2}}\;\equiv\;\frac{2\pi}{\tau_{\mathrm{b}}},\label{eq:phi_dot_ave}\end{equation}

\end_inset

 from which we obtain Eq.
\begin_inset space ~
\end_inset

(
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "eq:tau_d_xi"

\end_inset

) in the deeply-trapped limit (where 
\begin_inset Formula $g\rightarrow1$
\end_inset

).
\end_layout

